   "text": "**Step 33 plan: classifier with the long-stroke features added.** Step 32 decoded cleanly. Presence of a long vertical stroke in cell column 3, by row 0\u20133:\n\n| Digit | Row 0 | Row 1 | Row 2 | Row 3 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 3% | 39% | 22% | 0% |\n| 1 | 1% | 0% | 0% | 0% |\n| 2 | 10% | 19% | 2% | 0% |\n| 3 | 0% | 3% | 7% | 1% |\n| 4 | 17% | 25% | 12% | 8% |\n| 5 | 0% | 0% | 5% | 1% |\n| 6 | 0% | 0% | 4% | 0% |\n| 7 | 0% | 13% | 9% | 3% |\n| 8 | 1% | 1% | 2% | 0% |\n| 9 | 0% | 9% | 15% | 9% |\n\nThe long right side of a 0 shows in 39% of 0s at row 1 against about 1% of 8s and 0% of 5s, which are two of the digits 0 still gets confused with.\n\nI now have 20 measured long-stroke features: vertical in columns 1\u20133 and horizontal in the top and bottom rows. This step is the step-27 classifier plus a presence/absence vote on those 20 features:\n\n- **Form:** same as the ordinary presence vote, using the measured frequencies.\n- **Scale:** 0.3.\n- **Clipping:** frequencies are clipped at 1.5% so the many near-zero entries do not produce extreme weights.\n- **Biases:** kept as in step 27; I will re-tune them once I see how the new features shift the class balance.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport math\n\n\ndef build_weights():\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # conv1: 4 oriented line detectors x 2 thresholds  (unchanged)\n    #   channel k   (k=0..3): orientation k, bias -t0\n    #   channel k+4         : same filter,  bias -t1\n    #   orientation 0: horizontal stroke, 1: \"/\" , 2: vertical, 3: \"\\\"\n    #   pooled(k) - pooled(k+4) = clip(resp - t0, 0, t1 - t0)  -> saturated map M_k\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    prof = np.array([-0.75, 0.25, 1.0, 0.25, -0.75])   # across-stroke profile (zero sum)\n    Hf = np.tile(prof[:, None], (1, 5))                # horizontal stroke detector\n    Vf = Hf.T.copy()                                   # vertical stroke detector\n    dv = [1.0, 0.4, -0.45, -0.9, -0.95]                # diagonal profile by |offset| (zero sum)\n    D1 = np.zeros((5, 5))\n    D2 = np.zeros((5, 5))\n    for r in range(5):\n        for c in range(5):\n            D1[r, c] = dv[abs((r - 2) + (c - 2))]      # \"/\" : ridge on r + c = 4\n            D2[r, c] = dv[abs((r - 2) - (c - 2))]      # \"\\\" : ridge on r = c\n    filts = [Hf, D1, Vf, D2]\n    t0, t1 = 0.45, 0.75\n    w1 = np.zeros((8, 1, 5, 5))\n    b1 = np.zeros(8)\n    for k in range(4):\n        w1[k, 0] = filts[k] / 5.0\n        b1[k] = -t0\n        w1[k + 4, 0] = filts[k] / 5.0\n        b1[k + 4] = -t1\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # conv2:\n    #   channels 0..3  : EH_k = ReLU(1 - amount/tau_h)  (\"no LONG stroke k here\")\n    #   channels 4..7  : E_k  = ReLU(1 - amount/tau)    (\"stroke k missing here\"; 0 = present)\n    #   channels 8..11 : unused\n    #   channels 12..15: stroke-end detectors (up, down, left, right)\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    k1 = np.array([0.5, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 0.5])\n    K2 = np.outer(k1, k1)\n    tau = 1.6\n    tau_h = 8.0\n    w2 = np.zeros((16, 8, 5, 5))\n    b2 = np.zeros(16)\n    for k in range(4):\n        w2[k, k] = -K2 / ((t1 - t0) * tau_h)           # heavy-stroke emptiness\n        w2[k, k + 4] = K2 / ((t1 - t0) * tau_h)\n        b2[k] = 1.0\n        w2[4 + k, k] = -K2 / ((t1 - t0) * tau)         # ordinary emptiness\n        w2[4 + k, k + 4] = K2 / ((t1 - t0) * tau)\n        b2[4 + k] = 1.0\n\n    def setM(ch, k, r, c, w):\n        # add weight w on the saturated orientation map M_k at kernel position (r, c)\n        w2[ch, k, r, c] += w / (t1 - t0)\n        w2[ch, k + 4, r, c] -= w / (t1 - t0)\n\n    HH, DS, VV, DB = 0, 1, 2, 3     # orientation indices: horizontal, \"/\", vertical, \"\\\"\n    INH = 4.0                       # strength of the \"nothing beyond the tip\" inhibition\n\n    # up-end (channel 12): tip at kernel (1,2), stroke continues to (2,2), nothing in row 0\n    for (r, wt) in [(1, 0.75), (2, 0.25)]:\n        setM(12, VV, r, 2, wt)\n        setM(12, DS, r, 2, 0.5 * wt)\n        setM(12, DB, r, 2, 0.5 * wt)\n    for c in (1, 2, 3):\n        for k in range(4):\n            setM(12, k, 0, c, -INH)\n        setM(12, HH, 1, c, -INH)\n\n    TIPD = 0.6      # weight of a diagonal stroke at the tip (down/left/right detectors)\n\n    # down-end (channel 13)\n    setM(13, VV, 3, 2, 0.75)\n    setM(13, DS, 3, 2, TIPD)\n    setM(13, DB, 3, 2, TIPD)\n    setM(13, VV, 2, 2, 0.25)\n    setM(13, DS, 2, 2, 0.125)\n    setM(13, DB, 2, 2, 0.125)\n    for c in (1, 2, 3):\n        for k in range(4):\n            setM(13, k, 4, c, -INH)\n        setM(13, HH, 3, c, -INH)\n\n    # left-end (channel 14)\n    setM(14, HH, 2, 1, 0.75)\n    setM(14, DS, 2, 1, TIPD)\n    setM(14, DB, 2, 1, TIPD)\n    setM(14, HH, 2, 2, 0.25)\n    setM(14, DS, 2, 2, 0.125)\n    setM(14, DB, 2, 2, 0.125)\n    for r in (1, 2, 3):\n        for k in range(4):\n            setM(14, k, r, 0, -INH)\n        setM(14, VV, r, 1, -INH)\n\n    # right-end (channel 15)\n    setM(15, HH, 2, 3, 0.75)\n    setM(15, DS, 2, 3, TIPD)\n    setM(15, DB, 2, 3, TIPD)\n    setM(15, HH, 2, 2, 0.25)\n    setM(15, DS, 2, 2, 0.125)\n    setM(15, DB, 2, 2, 0.125)\n    for r in (1, 2, 3):\n        for k in range(4):\n            setM(15, k, r, 4, -INH)\n        setM(15, VV, r, 3, -INH)\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Measured presence frequencies (percent) of the E-channel features.\n    # Layout: [digit][cell row][cell column].  None = not measured (weight 0).\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    N = None\n    H_tab = [   # horizontal stroke present  (cell (0,3) is a rough estimate)\n        [[7.6, 55, 86, 60], [3.7, 17, 20.8, 11.5], [3.8, 9.4, 14.7, 8.7], [53.5, 96.9, 88.9, 37.2]],   # 0\n        [[0.5, 2, 1.7, 2], [0.6, 